ck downstream calls use the gateway's own credentials. 4) Answer no if any claim is unchecked, signature verification is disabled, or the caller's `Authorization` header is forwarded downstream.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Gateway token validation is outside this repo.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## E06.3\n\n**Check:** The gateway authorizes each action, validates requests and responses, enforces rate limits, and logs every decision.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open the gateway's request handling. 2) Check per-action authorization, request and response validation, rate limits, and a log entry for every decision. 3) Answer no if any is missing, authorization happens only once per connection, or denials are not logged.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Gateway authorization, validation, rate limits and decision logs are outside this repo.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## E06.4\n\n**Check:** If a required check (policy engine, scanner, token check) errors or times out, the call is blocked.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, and timeout around the policy engine, scanner, and token check. 2) Check each error blocks the call. 3) Answer no if any error branch allows the call or logs and continues, or a config flag defaults to fail-open.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Gateway fail-closed behavior is outside this repo; the client raises on RPC errors (mcp_client.py:83).\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## E06.5\n\n**Check:** Requests whose routing headers (such as Mcp-Name) don't match the body are rejected before policy, and cached tool lists and responses are stored per authorization context.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find where routing or policy reads headers such as `Mcp-Name`. 2) Check the header is compared with the body before policy runs, and mismatches are rejected. 3) Check tool-list and response caches are keyed by authorization context. 4) Answer no if headers are trusted without the compare, or a cache is shared across callers.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Header and body matching and per-context caches live in the gateway; the client's tool-list cache is global, not per authorization context.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## E06.6\n\n**Check:** If the gateway is itself an OAuth client, it checks the authorization server's issuer (iss, RFC 9207) and blocks private and metadata addresses in discovery URLs. Answer yes with the code line, or yes citing the config that shows it isn't an OAuth client.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Check whether the gateway acts as an OAuth client (gets tokens, follows discovery or metadata URLs). 2) If so, check it verifies the `iss` parameter (RFC 9207) and blocks private, loopback, and metadata addresses (169.254.169.254) in discovery URLs. 3) Answer no if either is missing. If it is not an OAuth client, answer yes citing the config that shows that.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Whether the gateway is an OAuth client is not shown in this repo.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to E06.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"E06\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"E06.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55264490-d981-452f-9884-d0f8